<div class="container mt-4">
  <%- include('../partials/breadcrumbs', { items: [{ name: 'Safety Tips' }] }) %>
  <article class="card card-pad prose">
    <h1>Safety Tips</h1>
    <p class="muted">Buying and selling locally is usually friendly and safe. A few simple habits keep it that way.</p>

    <h2>Meeting in person</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Meet in a busy, well-lit public place during the day.</li>
      <li>Take a friend or family member along.</li>
      <li>Tell someone where you are going and when you expect to be back.</li>
      <li>Trust your instincts &mdash; if something feels wrong, walk away.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Inspect the item before you pay.</li>
      <li>Prefer cash or a secure, traceable method on collection.</li>
      <li>Never send deposits, gift cards or cryptocurrency to someone you haven't met.</li>
      <li>Be wary of prices that are too good to be true.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Spotting scams</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Requests to move the chat off-platform immediately.</li>
      <li>Overpayment offers, or "shipping agents" for a local item.</li>
      <li>Pressure to pay quickly or pay before seeing the item.</li>
      <li>Sellers who refuse an inspection.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you spot a scam or a prohibited listing, use the <strong>Report this ad</strong> button on the ad. Our moderators review every report.</p>

    <h2>Selling safely</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep your email private &mdash; use our relay contact form.</li>
      <li>Remove any personal details from photos (number plates, documents, house numbers).</li>
      <li>Ask buyers to confirm a time before meeting.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Emergencies</h2>
    <p>In an emergency, always contact your local emergency services first (in Australia, call <strong>000</strong>).</p>
  </article>
</div>
